    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `build_client` in `app/llm_client.py`, and all four requirements work when checked against a stub transport.\n\nOne thing to know first: the pinned `openai==3.19.2` uses **`httpx2`**, not `httpx`. So the HTTP client, timeout and event hook all come from `httpx2`, which is already installed as a dependency of `openai`. Nothing was added or installed.\n\n```python\nTIMEOUT = httpx2.Timeout(30.0, connect=5.0)\nMAX_RETRIES = 2\n\ndef _log_request(request: httpx2.Request) -> None:\n    logger.info(\"%s %s\", request.method, request.url)\n\ndef build_client(api_key: str, transport=None) -> OpenAI:\n    http_client = DefaultHttpxClient(\n        timeout=TIMEOUT,\n        transport=transport,\n        event_hooks={\"request\": [_log_request]},\n    )\n    return OpenAI(api_key=api_key, timeout=TIMEOUT, max_retries=MAX_RETRIES, http_client=http_client)\n```\n\n- **Timeouts:** I set them on both the `OpenAI` client and the HTTP client. The SDK attaches its own timeout to every request, so setting it only on the HTTP client wouldn't be enough.\n- **Client defaults:** `DefaultHttpxClient` keeps the SDK's usual connection limits and redirect-following. Passing `transport=None` means it uses the normal transport.\n- **Logging:** the `\"request\"` event hook runs on every attempt, so retries are logged too.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `pytest -q`: 1 passed.\n- A stub `httpx2.MockTransport` that returns a 500 and then a 200 showed:\n  - two `INFO:app.http:GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models` lines (the first attempt and the retry);\n  - `max_retries == 2`;\n  - each request carried `connect=5.0, read=30.0, write=30.0, pool=30.0`.\n\nI couldn't delete the temporary `smoke_check.py` I created in the project root because the deletion wasn't approved. It's safe to remove."
